Slax is built on amd64 Debian. The target system is created with debootstrap;
package installation and cleanup run inside its AUFS root, not on the host.

Run as root from the repository:

    sh Slax/debian13/build trixie

The first run compiles and installs the pinned Slax kernel. Reboot into that
kernel and run the same command again to build Slax. The host and Slax use
the same kernel and modules. AUFS is built into the kernel.

Mount /tmp as tmpfs to build in RAM (20 GB recommended). Kernel compilation
and the entire Slax build use /tmp. Completed Slax build directories are kept
for further edits; their paths are printed at the end. Failed Slax builds and
kernel compilation remove their temporary files. The production kernel has
no DWARF or BTF debug information.

An optional second argument selects the working directory. The default is
/var/tmp/slax-build-trixie. Keep it on a Linux filesystem with enough free
space for the finished kernel packages and ISO. Compiler packages are not
included in Slax.

The finished slax-amd64.iso (BIOS and UEFI) and package lists in manifests
are saved to the working directory. A new run reuses the compiled kernel.
